course: dictionary
lesson: 429
title: Words that name a place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Arabian is a word that tells you where something comes from or belongs to. The word Arabia names a large peninsula in south-west Asia, so Arabian means to do with Arabia or its people. Look at the clues around the word to find this.
explain: «Many of the world's biggest hot deserts, such as the Sahara, the Arabian and the Australian deserts, lie at about 20 to 30 degrees north or south of the equator.» The Sahara and the Australian deserts are places, so the Arabian desert is a place too. Try the swap: put "the Arabia desert" in the sentence. It still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Arabian can also come before a noun that is not a place. «A "Djinn" (genie) is a magic spirit from Arabian stories.» The stories come from Arabia, and a "Djinn" is a magic spirit in them. Words like Arabian Nights and Arabian horse work the same way: the first word tells you where the thing is from or what kind it is.
fact: Arabian means to do with Arabia, the large peninsula in south-west Asia, or its people.
fact: An Arabian horse is a fast, graceful breed of horse.
fact: Arabian is also used in names such as Arabian Peninsula, Arabian Sea, and Arabian Nights.
fact: «Arabian» is a proper noun when it names a place, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: The Arabian oryx is an animal that was brought back from the brink, as «the Arabian oryx» shows.
exercise: «Many of the world's biggest hot deserts, such as the Sahara, the Arabian and the Australian deserts, lie at about 20 to 30 degrees north or south of the equator.» What does Arabian name here? | A kind of camel | *A desert in the region of Arabia | A cold country in the north | The name of a sea
exercise: What is an Arabian horse? | *A fast, graceful breed of horse | A horse that cannot run | A small pony with short legs | A horse from a circus
exercise: «A "Djinn" (genie) is a magic spirit from Arabian stories.» What is a Djinn? | A desert | *A magic spirit | A camel
test: «The Arabian oryx was hunted to extinction in the wild by 1972.» In this sentence, what does Arabian tell us about the oryx? | *It belongs to the Arabia region | It is a kind of fish | It has a long tail | It is very small
test: What is the Arabian Peninsula? | A kind of sea creature | *A large peninsula in south-west Asia | A small island in the Pacific | A city in Europe
exam: In «the Arabian oryx», what does Arabian mean? | A type of desert in Africa | *To do with Arabia, the large peninsula in south-west Asia | A colour of sand | The oldest kind of oryx
